
Closes #47.

This PR adds a new maintainer guide: docs/feedback-to-case-study.md.

The guide explains how maintainers can turn feedback issues into anonymized case studies that are safe to publish and useful for future users.

## Changes

- Add a step-by-step workflow for converting feedback issues into case studies
- Define what information should be extracted from feedback
- Add privacy and sensitive information handling rules
- Provide a reusable case study structure
- Add a pre-publish checklist for maintainers

## Why

Feedback issues often contain useful real-world usage signals, but they may also include private project details, user identities, logs, internal URLs, tokens, or organization-specific context.

This guide helps maintainers preserve the reusable learning value while removing sensitive information before publishing the case as documentation.

## Validation

- [ ] Markdown lint passes
- [ ] The guide includes privacy and sensitive information rules
- [ ] The guide can be copied by maintainers as a repeatable workflow
- [ ] The case study structure is clear enough for future contributors to reuse

